# Compile-time code computes for the selected target, not for the compiler's
# host. Hosted, the `#run` value of `sys.usize_max()` is the 64-bit maximum the
# program computes at run time. Checked for `board.sensor_v1` and for `web`,
# both 32-bit, the same value is the 32-bit maximum, so the narrow program's
# check passes; checked hosted, the same program measures 64-bit pointers and
# stops with E3010.
fixture: ComptimeDiffHostTargetValuesFollowTheTargetLayout.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "64 18446744073709551615 18446744073709551615\n"
step: jet check --target=board.sensor_v1 narrow.jet
exit: 0
step: jet check --target=web narrow.jet
exit: 0
step: jet check narrow.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "compile-time code measured 64-bit pointers for a 32-bit target" # the hosted check measures the host's width
